To answer your question: What are you supposed to do (about floating
eyes) if you've explored the dungeon down to this point and haven't
found a source of reflection yet?  Answer: don't smack the darn
things!  They're slow and harmless so long as you don't hit one in
melee.  If you absolutely have to kill one of the things you can throw
darts you found lying around, or zap it with a wand of spell.

Actually, in pre-Sokoban Nethack, and post-Sokoban Nethack for those
games with a bag of holding as the reward, reflection isn't all *that*
common at level 13.  It was actually rather rare by that time, in that
its only sources are silver dragon scales, silver dragon scale mail,
amulets of reflection and polished silver shields.  Two of those are
likely only available by wishing by that point, and the others are
subject to the whims of the randon number generation.  Reflection is a
lower priority than magic resistance, because you can win easily (or
without much additional trouble) without it, but the Wizard will
finger-of-death your ass without magic resistance.

